{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016899-folding-abilities-into-other-abilities","id":1016899,"title":"Folding abilities into other abilities?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-13T21:03:10-08:00","id":1016899,"title":"Folding abilities into other abilities?","content":"Hi there. <br /> <br /> I'm about to start a new M20 campaign and I decided to unify some abilities, so Id like to hear some opinions about it. <br /> <br /> Im thinking about using Occult with a necessary specialty, like Academicism, Science and the like. Im thinking about using Cosmology as an Occult specialty in that fashion. <br /> <br /> Im thinking about ditching Arts and Performance to use just Expression and Crafts. Crafts for arts that include using your hands or any part of your body to modify some material - painting, sculpting, weaving, etc - and Expression for arts like singing, dancing, writing and the like. I guess Expression would have some necessary specialty too. <br /> <br /> Ive put Laws and Politics together into Bureaucracy. <br /> <br /> I dont know what to do with Technology. Should I fold it into Crafts, maybe? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T22:10:15-08:00","id":1016910,"title":"","content":"To answer your question it would be helpful to know what you want accomplished.<br /> <br /> You can cut abilities completely and just go with physical social and mental, if you want.<br /> <br /> There are things worse than a merge of Art and Technology into Crafts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T22:49:49-08:00","id":1016920,"title":"","content":"I personally find the M20 Ability list bloated and like to trim it down as well. But as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12022_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12022\" data-vbnamecard=\"12022\">Nonsense</a> said, it's best to have a goal in mind beyond that to pick what you want to trim down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T05:41:29-08:00","id":1017002,"title":"","content":"Reducing the abilities list to 30 or 33 at most is my main goal. My list goes like this, without the modifications Ive thought about. I still use some old abilities and Ive included some you normally dont use in WoD, but in games like Exalted. <br /> <br /> TALENTS<br /> <br /> Arts<br /> Athletics<br /> Awareness (Alertness included here)<br /> Dodge (still use it)<br /> Empathy<br /> Endurance (internal resistance)<br /> Expression<br /> Intimidation<br /> Intuition<br /> Leadership<br /> Streetwise<br /> Subterfuge<br /> <br /> SKILLS<br /> <br /> Animal Ken<br /> Brawl / Martial Arts<br /> Crafts<br /> Drive<br /> Etiquette<br /> Firearms<br /> Larceny<br /> Melee<br /> Meditation<br /> Technology<br /> Stealth<br /> Survival<br /> <br /> KNOWLEDGE<br /> <br /> Academics<br /> Bureaucracy (politics and law)<br /> Computer<br /> Cosmology<br /> Finance<br /> Investigation<br /> Linguistics (still use it; I dont use merits)<br /> Lore (general knowledge about something, not necessarily supernatural, that couldnt be covered by other abilities)<br /> Medicine<br /> Occult<br /> Science<br /> Tactics (this one is about militar strategy and all of that)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T06:40:00-08:00","id":1017034,"title":"","content":"I dont understand why you continue to use Dodge instead of making it an Athletics specialty if you are trying to trim things down. Also, Alertness and Awarness are nothing close to the same thing. And hasn't Larrceny sorta been rolled in to Technology in M20? I realize its a bit wierd for simple lockpicking but not that to the point of being an issue. Other aspects of what Larceny deals with, money laundering and what have you would easily fit in Law/Politics or your Bureaucracy (which I do like).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T07:27:06-08:00","id":1017052,"title":"","content":"Youre right, Im open to fold anything now, so I could do it with Dodge too. <br /> <br /> In my version of the game, mages have a sort of sixth sense for the sake of being awakened. So thats it: no big deal. Not necessary to have one ability to perceive physical things and another one to perceive supernatural things. <br /> <br /> So, Technology for lockpicking?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T08:10:34-08:00","id":1017071,"title":"","content":"Ya. I see why they use Technology for lockpicking because all security alarms and what not fit under it, and possibly computers as well. It just seems odd if you old school lockpick with actual picks, but even then its not that far of a stretch. Just combine with Dex instead of Intelligence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T13:29:18-08:00","id":1017268,"title":"","content":"Personally, I've folded every Secondary Ability into one or more of the Primary Abilities, either as specialties or as Academics-like fields. For instance, Archery and Energy Weapons are variants of Firearms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T09:09:46-08:00","id":1017678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016899-folding-abilities-into-other-abilities?p=1017268#post1017268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I've folded every Secondary Ability into one or more of the Primary Abilities, either as specialties or as Academics-like fields. For instance, Archery and Energy Weapons are variants of Firearms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, yup.<br /> <br /> I did that pretty much holistically for our current M20 game. <br /> <br /> Flying, High Ritual, Lucid Dreaming, Search, Seduction, Acrobatics, Archery, Biotech, Energy Weapons, Hypertech, Jetpack, Riding, Torture, Belief Systems, Cryptography, Demolitions, Lore/RD Data, Media, Pharmacopeia/Poisons all got folded into relevant Abilities. They all became specialties (which can be bought before 4 dots)<br /> <br /> However, I added Finance and Pilot to the Ability list. And dug into V20 to add in Larceny and Performance. As well as the 3 &quot;none of the above, but seems like a separate Talent/Skill/Knowledge&quot; generic at the end. <br /> <br /> Do and Blatancy were liquidated with extreme prejudice. <br /> <br /> Some of that had to do with the aesthetics of wanting there to be the same number on each list. Very OCD, but there it is.<br /> <br /> Looking back I could probably have trimmed it down a little more, but I really think Finance needs to be a full on Ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T08:58:27-08:00","id":1018824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016899-folding-abilities-into-other-abilities?p=1017678#post1017678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some of that had to do with the aesthetics of wanting there to be the same number on each list. Very OCD, but there it is.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Same here. <br /> <br /> What was your final list?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T00:35:57-08:00","id":1022646,"title":"","content":"Awareness and Intuition are very similar. I'd merge those and keep Alertness separate. <br /> <br /> Arts would fall under Crafts or Expression. Cosmology and Lore I'd put under Occult. Endurance you probably don't need (you can roll Stamina + Survival). Tactics seems a bit niche. I'd roll it into Leadership. I also second making Dodge part of Athletics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T02:56:18-08:00","id":1022665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1016899-folding-abilities-into-other-abilities?p=1022646#post1022646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awareness and Intuition are very similar. I'd merge those and keep Alertness separate. <br /> <br /> Arts would fall under Crafts or Expression. Cosmology and Lore I'd put under Occult. Endurance you probably don't need (you can roll Stamina + Survival). Tactics seems a bit niche. I'd roll it into Leadership. I also second making Dodge part of Athletics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cosmology and occult are quite distinct though. One is about all things umbra, from spirits to the various realms. The three worlds, knowledge on the various hierarchies between the differing categories of spirit. The power of Wraiths and the world of the Dreaming. As well as a few things about deep Umbral space. <br /> The other is about all things magick, from ritualsand tools, gods and legends, to knowledge on spheres and rotes you don't posess, along with knowledge of other tradition's mystic practices and their more famous members.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 12-27-2016, 06:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}